DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstantFunctions=>0);
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstants=>0);

$fun_2 = Formula("((x^2+5*x+2))^2");
$fun_1 = Formula("cos((x^2))");

Context("Interval");

$set_ans_3 = Compute("[0, infinity) U [2, infinity) U [2, infinity) - ((-infinity, infinity) - [2, infinity))");
$set_ans_4 = Compute("([2, infinity) U ([0, infinity))) U ([0, infinity) - ((-infinity, infinity) - [0, infinity))) U ([2, infinity) U {-7, -3, 0, 1, 2} U {-7, -3, 0, 1, 2}) U [0, infinity) U ([0, infinity) U {-7, -3, 0, 1, 2})");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("{-10, -3} U (-infinity, 17)");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("(-infinity, 17) U ((-infinity, 15])");

Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

- _For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._
- _For derivative problems, if the result is undefined, then *leave the blank empty*._

[`15+8-8`] is equal to [_____]{answer=>Real(15.),width=>3}
---

[`7+16+19*5`] is equal to [_____]{answer=>Formula('118'),width=>3}
---

What is the value of [`15+7-19+13*4`]? [_____]{answer=>55,width=>7}
---

What is the value of [`17+3-4-12*12`]? [_____]{answer=>Formula('-128'),width=>9}
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{x | x \leq 15\}`]
- [`B = \{x | x < 17\}`]
- [`C = \{-10, -3\}`]

Compute:
- [`C \cup B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`B \cup (A) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}

---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{x | x \geq 0\}`]
- [`B = \{-7, -3, 0, 1, 2\}`]
- [`C = \{x | x \geq 2\}`]

Compute:
- [`A \cup C \cup C \cap C = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}
- [`(C \cup (A)) \cup (A \cap A) \cup (C \cup B \cup B) \cup A \cup (A \cup B) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -3, 9, -8 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 7, 1, 1 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle -3, 10, 10 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-3, 9, -8>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-3, 9, -8>") . Compute("<7, 1, 1>")}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<-3, 9, -8>"))}
- [` \vec{u} \times \vec{w} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-3, 9, -8>") x Compute("<-3, 10, 10>")}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{w} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-3, 10, 10>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -3, -1, -2 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -10, 7, -5 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle 10, 8, 5 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-3, -1, -2>") . Compute("<-10, 7, -5>")}
- [` \vec{v} \cdot \vec{w} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-10, 7, -5>") . Compute("<10, 8, 5>")}
- [` \vec{v} \times \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-10, 7, -5>") x Compute("<-3, -1, -2>")}
- [` \vec{v} \times \vec{w} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-10, 7, -5>") x Compute("<10, 8, 5>")}
- [` \left\| \vec{v} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-10, 7, -5>"))}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_1]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->D()}
- [`f'(4) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>4)}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_2]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}
- [`f'(0) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>0)}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->D()}
- [`f'(8) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>8)}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
